  "description": "Ænima is the second studio album by the American rock band Tool. It was released on vinyl on September 17, 1996, and on cassette and compact disc on October 1, 1996, through Zoo and Volcano Entertainment. Produced by the band and David Bottrill, the album was recorded at Ocean Way Recording in Hollywood and The Hook in North Hollywood. It is the first album by Tool to feature bassist Justin Chancellor, who replaced original bassist Paul D'Amour the year prior.",
